hexagon: htp: v81 uses the f32 to f16 conversion of v79

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

hvx_vec_f32_to_f16_shuff (htp/hvx-base.h) gave v81 the conversion
Vqf32 = Vsf, an instruction that only v81 has. v79 multiplies by 1.0 into
qf32. With this patch v81 also multiplies by 1.0. No silicon of this project
executed Vqf32 = Vsf, and the v79 silicon verified the multiply form.

The kernel lab (tools/htp-lab, the release flags of the DSP library, the
core v81na_2: 12 threads, 8 HVX contexts, 8 MB VTCM):
  - target f16rne: each of the two forms gives the round to nearest even of
    the CPU for the 862208 values of the sweep and the 25 special values (a
    NaN gives a NaN). A copy of 2560 values takes 411.8 to 411.9 cycles
    with each form.
  - target gdnk (the chunked GATED_DELTA_NET, the HVX part, 2 heads of 128,
    64 tokens, 2 threads): 716725 cycles with Vqf32 = Vsf, 719517 cycles
    with the multiply (+0.4 %).
  - The HVX census (tools/htp-lab/isa, v79na_1 against v81na_2): the
    multiply form gives the same bits on v79 and v81, also for a NaN. Each
    qf32 and qf16 operation and each conversion to IEEE gives the same bits
    on the two cores.
  - The HMX census (tools/htp-lab/hmxisa): the same bytes on v75, v79 and v81
    for each HMX mode.

The float instructions (tools/htp-lab/inventory/archdiff.py):
  - Without this patch, 28 functions of the Qwen3.5 ops have other float
    instructions on v81 than on v79: 410 sites of Vqf32 = Vsf.
  - With this patch, each function of the Qwen3.5 ops has the float
    instructions of v79. The other differences are moves, loads, stores and
    nops. The one v81 form that stays is Vqf32 = Vsf in the f16 DIV of the
    binary jobs (96 sites), where the compiler lowers Q6_Vhf_vcvt_VsfVsf.
    The Qwen3.5 graph has no f16 DIV.

The v79 library keeps its bytes: libggml-htp-v79.so has the SHA-256
61c028af9bb1f3622d5502e1af43c7ce2f1da4f24e0bf3d0707a00494f35e606 with and
without this patch (tools/stages/v81/build.sh, the flags of the app build).

No v81 silicon verified this patch.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/hvx-base.h b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/hvx-base.h
index 99c8e0e..3624dc7 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/hvx-base.h
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/hvx-base.h
@@ -122,14 +122,16 @@ static inline HVX_VectorPred hvx_vec_is_nan_f16(HVX_Vector v) {
 }
 
 // The f16 values of two f32 vectors. On v79 and v81 the result is the IEEE conversion with round to
-// nearest even, the conversion of the CPU backend. On v79 the multiply by 1.0 keeps the sign of a
-// zero, where an add of 0 gives +0 for -0. Before v79 the qf32 to hf conversion rounds a tie up,
-// and it gives a NaN for an Inf (tools/htp-lab, target f16rne).
+// nearest even, the conversion of the CPU backend. The multiply by 1.0 keeps the sign of a zero,
+// where an add of 0 gives +0 for -0. Before v79 the qf32 to hf conversion rounds a tie up, and it
+// gives a NaN for an Inf (tools/htp-lab, target f16rne).
+//
+// v81 also has the conversion Vqf32 = Vsf. In the v81 simulator it gives the same bits as the
+// multiply for all values of the target f16rne, and a copy loop takes the same cycles. v81 uses the
+// multiply, thus the v81 library has the float instruction forms of the v79 library, which the v79
+// silicon verified. Vqf32 = Vsf is an instruction that no silicon of this project executed.
 static inline HVX_Vector hvx_vec_f32_to_f16_shuff(HVX_Vector v0, HVX_Vector v1) {
-#if __HVX_ARCH__ >= 81
-    HVX_Vector q0 = Q6_Vqf32_equals_Vsf(v0);
-    HVX_Vector q1 = Q6_Vqf32_equals_Vsf(v1);
-#elif __HVX_ARCH__ >= 79
+#if __HVX_ARCH__ >= 79
     const HVX_Vector one = hvx_vec_splat_f32(1.0f);
     HVX_Vector q0 = Q6_Vqf32_vmpy_VsfVsf(v0, one);
     HVX_Vector q1 = Q6_Vqf32_vmpy_VsfVsf(v1, one);
